Z||000005||ray b||01-29-2001||07:02 PM|||| older 3-486 laptops are cheap slow but email speed should be ok. big computer mags have adds for used stuff in back or try goodwill tipe stores or gov. surplus.  ray||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||01-29-2001||10:58 PM||||There are some pretty cheap laptops around now. might be a better deal just to buy one. If a leased one is swiped you are still responcible for the whole lease PLUS the buyout. You could easily spend 3 times what the thing is worth.<P>Rules and regulations reguarding strong encryption, 64 bit and higher, have been changed. Also these laws mainly apply to product being sold outside the U.S.. For details contact U.S. Customs or the Commerce Department. You can also try asking the PGP or RSA people. Generally as long as you aren't traveling to a country on the resticted list there probably isn't a problem but check with customs anyway. The restricted list is always changing and Kosovo may be on it.<P>Now if the term vacation is sarcasm..... you need to check mil regs. Those are way differant. Taking an unapproved laptop thru military channels to various countries could get you tossed in jail for a long time. Things a normal person can do with encryption aren't the same as military personel no matter what Commerce says. If you aren't 100% sure ask. Better to get told no now than end up in the brig.<P>as for programs AOL and IE both install with 128 bit encryption. Instant messenger doesn't use encryption but may violate other regs. Check around and CYA.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||pHoOl||01-29-2001||11:24 PM||||Couldn't have said it better myself<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
